# Knowledge base

What is true about this project beyond what the code says: structure,
vocabulary, workflows and the reasons behind them. Agents load this index on
demand from the entry file; keep it to one line per topic.

## Topics

- [Architecture](architecture.md): components, dependency direction, trust boundaries.
- [Glossary](glossary.md): project terms, one meaning each.
- [Flows](flows.md): ordered steps of the main workflows.
- [Decisions](decisions/): numbered decision records with status.
- [Lessons](../../memories/lessons.md): dated, evidenced lessons.
- [Plans](../plans/): multi-session work in progress.

## Where new knowledge goes

| You learned | Put it in |
| --- | --- |
| A command, version or path | the project facts file |
| How components fit together now | architecture |
| What a term means | glossary |
| The steps of a workflow | flows |
| Why a costly choice was made | a new decision record |
| A surprising fact with evidence | the lessons file |
| State of unfinished work | the session handoff |

## Rules

- Link to owning code, tests and configuration; do not copy values.
- Supersede records; never delete or silently rewrite them.
- No secrets, personal data, transcripts or customer content.
- Re-verify entries whose linked files changed in the same change set.
- Run the memory checker before merging changes to these folders.
